WEBVTT

00:14.250 --> 00:15.670
Onee-chan...?

00:34.610 --> 00:36.270
Onee-chan's head...

00:36.780 --> 00:38.280
Her head is floating...

00:47.700 --> 00:56.470
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:56.510 --> 01:05.510
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

01:05.550 --> 01:12.280
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:14.890 --> 01:20.960
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:23.130 --> 01:31.700
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:31.740 --> 01:38.340
And I'm faced with another day

01:39.550 --> 01:45.280
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:45.320 --> 01:49.620
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:49.660 --> 01:54.100
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:54.130 --> 01:58.530
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:58.570 --> 02:03.060
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:03.110 --> 02:10.950
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:16.220 --> 02:20.350
MAIKUBI

02:16.220 --> 02:20.350
Dancing Severed Heads

02:26.000 --> 02:27.390
Jeez...

02:27.740 --> 02:32.750
I thought that if I went with them,
then I'd encounter some mysterious tales...

02:33.020 --> 02:34.900
These don't taste as good...

02:35.070 --> 02:38.900
They don't compare at all with
Kyougoku dumplings, of course.

02:38.990 --> 02:42.570
No, these are quite good.

02:42.660 --> 02:43.990
This is how it is, I guess.

03:06.060 --> 03:07.350
Are you okay?

03:08.640 --> 03:09.890
What happened?

03:10.980 --> 03:13.560
Save me, please!

03:21.240 --> 03:22.910
Umm...

03:32.080 --> 03:33.380
Hey, there he is!

03:42.130 --> 03:44.010
Stop!

03:49.270 --> 03:50.270
Umm...

03:51.690 --> 03:55.110
Thank you for saving me.

03:56.440 --> 03:57.980
Uh... no.

04:16.540 --> 04:19.710
Jeez... I can't watch this.

04:19.800 --> 04:22.300
Matanoji... that guy is...

04:22.510 --> 04:25.340
A very unlucky person.

04:28.390 --> 04:31.100
Is it really okay to leave him like this?

04:33.810 --> 04:36.100
Well, it has nothing to do with me, I guess.

05:01.920 --> 05:04.760
Momosuke-san, are you from Edo?

05:04.840 --> 05:06.220
Yes.

05:07.470 --> 05:08.640
Edo, eh?

05:09.060 --> 05:11.510
If you ever go there, please visit me.

05:11.770 --> 05:14.270
Look for the Ikomaya at the Kyobashi.

05:11.770 --> 05:15.940
[Note: Kyobashi is a bridge in Edo.]

05:15.940 --> 05:18.360
Oh? Are you the master of that large store?

05:19.180 --> 05:20.650
Well...

05:21.440 --> 05:23.990
Hmm? Otama, what's wrong?

05:24.820 --> 05:25.990
She's my sister.

05:28.570 --> 05:29.700
We have a guest.

05:30.490 --> 05:34.830
I was attacked by a brigand and that man saved me.

05:35.330 --> 05:36.750
Stay quiet, okay?

05:41.800 --> 05:44.340
I'm sorry, she's quite shy.

05:45.720 --> 05:46.880
It's okay.

05:47.470 --> 05:49.890
My sister is blind.

05:56.190 --> 05:59.690
Do you wonder how we can live like this?

05:59.940 --> 06:01.190
Well, umm...

06:01.360 --> 06:07.030
I'm the mistress of Yihei Anzai,
the head of a fisherman's group.

06:09.410 --> 06:10.820
There's no way around it...

06:18.080 --> 06:19.420
Hey, mister.

06:19.500 --> 06:20.830
What?

06:20.960 --> 06:23.300
What's your relationship to Oyoshi?

06:24.550 --> 06:25.710
I'm nothing at all to her.

06:25.840 --> 06:27.590
Why were you with her?

06:27.630 --> 06:29.550
Hey, he's hurt.

06:29.640 --> 06:31.430
What?

06:31.470 --> 06:35.640
Stop it. Scare him any more and he'll pee in his pants.

06:36.980 --> 06:39.640
I've got my eyes on that woman.

06:39.850 --> 06:42.440
Screw around and I'll kill you.

06:42.480 --> 06:44.110
The world's a scary place, you know.

06:44.190 --> 06:45.860
Better be careful!

06:47.740 --> 06:50.030
Do you think I'm alone?

06:54.910 --> 06:56.040
That's him?

07:03.340 --> 07:08.050
Does this inn happen to have any scary stories
about it that have been passed down from ancient times?

07:08.590 --> 07:10.300
Any ghosts appearing?

07:10.840 --> 07:12.390
This is your room.

07:13.970 --> 07:14.930
Here?

07:15.060 --> 07:16.350
Enjoy yourself.

07:20.480 --> 07:23.480
Jeez, what an unfriendly woman...

07:31.200 --> 07:32.450
Just my imagination?

07:32.490 --> 07:34.030
Looking for somebody?

07:36.120 --> 07:37.870
Mataichi-san!

07:37.950 --> 07:40.080
Oh. Hello there, sensei.

07:40.160 --> 07:41.960
I didnt expect to see you here.

07:42.500 --> 07:43.830
Didn't expect to?

07:44.710 --> 07:47.960
Mataichi-san, you didn't follow me here, did you?

07:48.090 --> 07:49.510
Don't kid yourself.

07:49.720 --> 07:51.550
Why the hell would we be following you?

07:51.680 --> 07:55.600
There aren't any other inns around here.

07:55.720 --> 07:57.970
Ogin-san? And Nagamimi san?

07:58.890 --> 08:02.560
But even so, there is a strange aura around this place.

08:02.690 --> 08:08.650
What? Could that possibly mean...
that there's a ghost here, too?

08:08.780 --> 08:10.610
Well now, sensei...

08:10.900 --> 08:14.160
Some things you're just better off not knowing.

08:14.280 --> 08:15.950
Please be clear!

08:16.080 --> 08:17.330
I knew it.

08:17.450 --> 08:19.370
You're going to say something, aren't you?

08:19.580 --> 08:20.290
What is it?

08:20.620 --> 08:22.160
I'm not going to get killed, am I?

08:30.590 --> 08:31.880
Oya, oya...

08:32.430 --> 08:35.550
He's very rude whenever he sees somebody's face, I guess.

08:35.600 --> 08:37.180
All the guts of a flea.

08:37.220 --> 08:38.970
Is he dead?

08:45.230 --> 08:47.810
Dinner will be ready soon, so just wait.

08:48.360 --> 08:49.770
I want to go outside.

08:49.900 --> 08:51.780
You can't! It's dangerous outside.

08:52.700 --> 08:57.530
It's your fault that I'm like this.

08:58.580 --> 09:00.490
It's all your fault.

09:01.700 --> 09:05.540
I know... so I'll do anything for you, Otama.

09:05.830 --> 09:06.960
Just words...

09:07.380 --> 09:08.210
That's not true...

09:09.210 --> 09:11.380
Oyoshi, are you there?

09:16.890 --> 09:18.090
Yahei-san.

09:18.510 --> 09:21.010
At a time like this... what happened?

09:21.350 --> 09:25.100
What? I just heard something that bothered me.

09:25.560 --> 09:32.860
The "Wanted Person" poster went around, but it'seems
there's an extremely strong Samurai still wandering about.

09:40.580 --> 09:43.410
It seems that even now he's hiding somewhere.

09:43.870 --> 09:45.000
Is that so?

09:45.330 --> 09:46.410
What's wrong?

09:46.580 --> 09:51.210
Nothing... if he's that terrifying,
then I hope they catch him quickly.

09:51.340 --> 09:52.500
That's right.

09:52.670 --> 09:56.260
Umm... Otama's condition doesn't look so good, and...

09:57.010 --> 09:59.050
How much do you want?

09:59.850 --> 10:02.810
Danna, did you come here
because you were worrying about me?

10:04.020 --> 10:05.980
Well, that too...

10:07.940 --> 10:10.900
Oh Danna... right here?

10:11.070 --> 10:15.740
I was so worried that now I can't control myself!

10:15.780 --> 10:16.490
Jeez...

10:23.490 --> 10:27.120
By that senile old man... by that bastard?

10:37.010 --> 10:38.380
Who are you?

10:39.010 --> 10:41.890
Your candle is burning out.

11:46.450 --> 11:47.580
Onee-chan...

11:51.750 --> 11:54.210
No, don't look...

11:54.540 --> 11:57.000
Your head... your head is floating...

12:11.640 --> 12:15.430
He looks like a little kid when he's sleeping.

12:17.020 --> 12:18.600
Matanoji?

12:19.180 --> 12:20.810
Such deep darkness...

12:37.450 --> 12:39.200
I'm back.

12:39.790 --> 12:40.870
Father!

12:45.170 --> 12:46.250
This scent...

12:47.170 --> 12:48.750
It's driving me crazy!

12:49.670 --> 12:52.510
Here... Otama will...

12:54.300 --> 12:56.180
Otama will awaken?

12:57.680 --> 12:59.350
Otama is here?

13:00.980 --> 13:02.060
In the next room...

13:04.020 --> 13:05.060
Wait!

13:09.320 --> 13:10.480
Please!

13:16.370 --> 13:17.410
Who are you?

13:17.740 --> 13:20.870
Just a paltry monk selling fuda.

13:21.410 --> 13:23.750
A monk selling fuda?

13:23.960 --> 13:25.420
I doubt that.

13:35.010 --> 13:36.470
Was he a mononoke?

13:36.680 --> 13:38.930
Father! It's dangerous here.

13:39.010 --> 13:43.310
Go to the temple at the edge of the village.
I'll meet you there tomorrow. I promise!

14:02.660 --> 14:04.370
What are you doing?

14:05.460 --> 14:08.500
Don't just walk into other people's rooms!

14:08.630 --> 14:11.710
Rubbing a towel against your cheeks and reminiscing...

14:11.960 --> 14:14.590
You're even more of a pervert than I thought.

14:15.760 --> 14:17.340
I can do that if I want!

14:18.350 --> 14:20.640
You're going back to Edo, right?

14:21.520 --> 14:23.430
I can do that if I want to, too!

14:23.600 --> 14:27.400
It'd be better for you if you did, I'm telling you.

14:34.070 --> 14:35.320
Wait...

14:35.400 --> 14:36.740
I fixed some food...

14:36.860 --> 14:38.610
I'll worry about that later.

14:40.200 --> 14:42.490
But you're so thin...

14:42.580 --> 14:43.540
Shut up!

14:55.220 --> 14:55.970
Oyoshi!

14:56.010 --> 14:56.920
I'm sorry!

14:58.840 --> 14:59.930
You...

15:00.180 --> 15:01.050
Forgive me!

15:01.140 --> 15:02.430
Please forgive me!

15:02.970 --> 15:06.560
Yahei-san... Yahei-san gave me these...

15:07.140 --> 15:09.150
That old man...

15:09.350 --> 15:12.980
He said that if I didn't kill you
then I couldn't stay in this village.

15:16.110 --> 15:18.030
Old man!

15:24.240 --> 15:26.950
Oyoshi! I killed the old man.

15:29.120 --> 15:30.370
Oyoshi!

15:45.600 --> 15:46.720
Otama?

15:51.270 --> 15:52.560
Do you know where Oyoshi is?

16:00.610 --> 16:01.530
Excuse me.

16:01.620 --> 16:02.700
Please come in.

16:04.080 --> 16:06.160
Good evening, Momosuke-san.

16:06.910 --> 16:09.620
Oyoshi-san? But why?

16:10.370 --> 16:14.210
Umm... I wanted to see you.

16:14.630 --> 16:16.630
I'm not intruding, am I?

16:17.510 --> 16:22.970
Me too... Um, I wanted to see you too, Oyoshi-san!

16:23.680 --> 16:25.260
What are you writing?

16:25.390 --> 16:31.230
Well, this is umm...a riddle... umm a story...

16:31.980 --> 16:33.310
You're a funny person.

16:37.110 --> 16:40.150
Oh, that's right! I need to return your towel.

16:41.200 --> 16:43.610
I don't care about that.

16:44.070 --> 16:45.320
But...

16:45.370 --> 16:48.080
I actually...

16:52.120 --> 16:53.710
Have a request.

16:55.130 --> 16:56.250
A request?

17:03.890 --> 17:04.510
Otama...

17:09.350 --> 17:11.060
This is terrible.

17:12.100 --> 17:13.310
Otama!

17:18.940 --> 17:20.480
Where are you, Otama?

17:22.030 --> 17:22.820
Otama!

17:24.950 --> 17:25.910
Oyoshi-san...

17:26.490 --> 17:27.660
Look at this.

17:27.830 --> 17:30.620
I have killed Yahei. Will wait at Yabuchi

17:31.120 --> 17:34.420
That man took Otama...

17:35.000 --> 17:36.250
Oyoshi-san, wait!

17:39.300 --> 17:40.550
You're...

17:43.300 --> 17:44.800
Sensei.

17:45.010 --> 17:48.390
Don't you think that it'd be better
if you didn't become more involved in this?

17:52.180 --> 17:56.270
Eh, I didn't think you'd stop.

18:04.200 --> 18:05.110
Oyoshi!

18:05.450 --> 18:08.620
Otama... give back Otama!

18:11.830 --> 18:14.870
Oyoshi-san, he's dangerous!

18:15.120 --> 18:19.040
Mr. Samurai, stop following Oyoshi-san!

18:19.210 --> 18:20.420
Give back Otama-chan!

18:20.670 --> 18:21.880
If you don't...

18:21.960 --> 18:24.170
Oyoshi, why?

18:24.260 --> 18:26.380
Why are you trying to run away from me?

18:26.680 --> 18:28.260
From your own father?

18:28.680 --> 18:29.760
Father?

18:31.680 --> 18:35.100
I've done everything for you!

18:35.390 --> 18:40.480
I've done everything for you...
no matter what you wanted!

18:42.070 --> 18:44.440
Kill mother.

18:45.450 --> 18:49.240
If you love me, then kill mother.

18:49.530 --> 18:50.490
Oyoshi...

18:50.700 --> 18:53.490
Kill mother...

18:57.210 --> 19:00.750
I've given you everything you wanted.

19:00.880 --> 19:03.800
No matter if I had to steal or kill!

19:03.920 --> 19:05.300
Lies!

19:05.920 --> 19:07.300
Give me back Otama!

19:09.390 --> 19:10.680
This?

19:13.140 --> 19:14.270
Otama!

19:21.110 --> 19:22.480
There, there...

19:22.570 --> 19:24.570
You must've been scared.

19:24.820 --> 19:26.780
Otama is no more.

19:26.990 --> 19:29.700
What are you saying? She's right here.

19:29.910 --> 19:32.030
Isn't that just a body?

19:37.960 --> 19:39.960
So it was you after all...

19:40.960 --> 19:46.460
Your head... your head and fathers head...

19:46.760 --> 19:47.970
You saw us, didn't you?

19:52.140 --> 19:53.550
Are you seared?

19:54.470 --> 19:57.730
Your sister was scared...

19:58.310 --> 20:00.140
Those eyes of yours...

20:04.520 --> 20:06.730
Otama... Otama is alive!

20:07.900 --> 20:11.110
Can you call this alive?

20:13.830 --> 20:15.870
You're Matajuro Ishikawa, aren't you?

20:16.200 --> 20:17.410
And if I am?

20:17.790 --> 20:19.710
We want you to give yourself up quietly to go hang.

20:35.970 --> 20:37.390
I won't die!

20:38.100 --> 20:39.640
I'll never die!

20:39.940 --> 20:41.600
I won't die.

20:41.980 --> 20:57.120
Sleep, sleep... I will protect you... I will protect you.....

20:57.950 --> 21:07.040
Good child...

21:04.750 --> 21:06.030
Oyoshi!

21:11.050 --> 21:14.430
His head... his head is floating...

21:22.640 --> 21:24.520
The heads...

21:28.480 --> 21:29.650
Why...

21:30.570 --> 21:34.280
It's something that you can never understand.

21:34.950 --> 21:37.370
That feeling...

21:40.910 --> 21:42.040
Mataichi-san...

21:44.460 --> 21:48.250
Will you release her from her suffering?

21:49.550 --> 21:52.920
I want to save her.

21:56.470 --> 21:58.720
You couldn't do such a difficult thing.

22:04.940 --> 22:07.810
The deed is done.

22:15.860 --> 22:21.950
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:23.300 --> 22:29.390
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:30.370 --> 22:36.140
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:36.180 --> 22:42.810
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:44.180 --> 22:50.120
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:50.160 --> 22:56.820
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:57.660 --> 23:07.130
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:08.440 --> 23:11.640
Draw near

23:11.910 --> 23:18.910
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:18.950 --> 23:24.890
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:27.060 --> 23:32.330
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:32.370 --> 23:41.000
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:52.400 --> 23:57.530
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:58.410 --> 24:03.350
The millionaire horse breeder,
Choujirou, chooses without revealing himself.

24:03.410 --> 24:06.330
Who will be tonight's dinner?

24:08.080 --> 24:12.290
Next time on Kyougoku
Natsuhiko's "Rumors 100 Stories",

24:12.580 --> 24:14.120
Shioya no Chouji

24:15.090 --> 24:17.640
The deed is done.
